{"questions":[{"question_id":"1lg1yg62t","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2007 Paper 1 Offline","year":2007,"examDate":2007,"subject":"physics","chapter":"dual-nature-of-radiation","chapterGroup":"modern-physics","topic":"photoelectric-effect","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"pstatement-1p-pif-the-accelerating-potential-in-an-x-jee-advanced-physics-motion-iwlf6lkzqkl2aylz","content":"<p><b>Statement 1 :</b></p>\n<p>If the accelerating potential in an X-ray tube is increased, the wavelengths of the characteristic X-rays do not change.</p>\n\n<p><b>Statement 2 :</b></p>\n<p>When an electron beam strikes the target in an X-ray tube, part of the kinetic energy is converted into X-ray energy.</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Statement 1 is True, Statement 2 is True, Statement 2 is a CORRECT explanation for Statement 1"},{"identifier":"B","content":"Statement 1 is True, Statement 2 is True, Statement 2 is NOT a CORRECT explanation for Statement 1"},{"identifier":"C","content":"Statement 1 is True, Statement 2 is False"},{"identifier":"D","content":"Statement 1 is False, Statement 2 is True"}],"correct_options":["B"],"explanation":"<p>Since, Potential increases</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1mggdcumc/d235f8a3-20a2-4f1b-b007-c95511411adf/a4180c40-a361-11f0-b814-0f72f73fa4cf/file-jaoe38c1mggdcumd.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/jaoe38c1mggdcumc/d235f8a3-20a2-4f1b-b007-c95511411adf/a4180c40-a361-11f0-b814-0f72f73fa4cf/file-jaoe38c1mggdcumd.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;max-height:40vh;vertical-align:baseline\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2007 Paper 1 Offline Physics - Dual Nature of Radiation Question 10 English Explanation 1\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/jaoe38c1mggdcumc/d235f8a3-20a2-4f1b-b007-c95511411adf/a4180c40-a361-11f0-b814-0f72f73fa4cf/file-jaoe38c1mggdcumd.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/jaoe38c1mggdcumc/d235f8a3-20a2-4f1b-b007-c95511411adf/a4180c40-a361-11f0-b814-0f72f73fa4cf/file-jaoe38c1mggdcumd.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1mggdcumc/d235f8a3-20a2-4f1b-b007-c95511411adf/a4180c40-a361-11f0-b814-0f72f73fa4cf/file-jaoe38c1mggdcumd.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/jaoe38c1mggdcumc/d235f8a3-20a2-4f1b-b007-c95511411adf/a4180c40-a361-11f0-b814-0f72f73fa4cf/file-jaoe38c1mggdcumd.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/jaoe38c1mggdcumc/d235f8a3-20a2-4f1b-b007-c95511411adf/a4180c40-a361-11f0-b814-0f72f73fa4cf/file-jaoe38c1mggdcumd.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/jaoe38c1mggdcumc/d235f8a3-20a2-4f1b-b007-c95511411adf/a4180c40-a361-11f0-b814-0f72f73fa4cf/file-jaoe38c1mggdcumd.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>If we give the constant energy release we observe constant wavelength. So the statement 1 is true.</p>\n<p>From Einstein equation,</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.8ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"15.132ex\" height=\"2.801ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -884.7 6688.5 1238.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(220,394) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"210E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-210E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(576,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D450\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D450\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(370.6,-345) scale